{"arm": "pinned:sclv/qwen3-next-80b", "requested_model": "sclv/qwen3-next-80b", "question_id": "8058", "dataset": "MMLU-Pro", "category": "math", "fold": "calibration", "started_at": 1787606230.875867, "latency_ms": 4888.448874997266, "http_status": 200, "attempts": 1, "error": null, "text": "To find the determinant of the 3×3 matrix:\n\n$$\nA = \\begin{bmatrix}\n0 & 1 & 2 \\\\\n7 & 8 & 3 \\\\\n6 & 5 & 4\n\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWe use the cofactor expansion along the first row:\n\n$$\n\\det(A) = 0 \\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}8 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{vmatrix}\n- 1 \\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}7 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 4\\end{vmatrix}\n+ 2 \\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}7 & 8 \\\\ 6 & 5\\end{vmatrix}\n$$\n\nCompute the 2×2 determinants:\n\n- First term: $0 \\cdot (8\\cdot4 - 3\\cdot5) = 0$\n- Second term: $-1 \\cdot (7\\cdot4 - 3\\cdot6) = -1 \\cdot (28 - 18) = -1 \\cdot 10 = -10$\n- Third term: $2 \\cdot (7\\cdot5 - 8\\cdot6) = 2 \\cdot (35 - 48) = 2 \\cdot (-13) = -26$\n\nNow sum:\n\n$$\n\\det(A) = 0 - 10 - 26 = -36\n$$\n\nSo the determinant is **-36**\n\nAnswer: I", "finish_reason": "stop", "served_model": "qwen3-next-80b", "prompt_tokens": 152, "completion_tokens": 321, "total_tokens": 473, "reasoning_tokens": null, "headers": {"vsr_selected_model": "sclv/qwen3-next-80b", "vsr_response_path": "upstream"}, "extracted": "I", "correct": true}
