{"arm": "pinned:sclv/qwen3-next-80b", "requested_model": "sclv/qwen3-next-80b", "question_id": "7952", "dataset": "MMLU-Pro", "category": "math", "fold": "test", "started_at": 1787606235.764987, "latency_ms": 6964.744333003182, "http_status": 200, "attempts": 1, "error": null, "text": "We are rolling six 6-sided dice and want the probability that **exactly three** show **prime numbers** and the **other three** show **composite numbers**.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Identify prime and composite numbers on a 6-sided die\n\nA 6-sided die has faces: **1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6**\n\nClassify them:\n\n- **Prime numbers**: 2, 3, 5 → 3 primes\n- **Composite numbers**: 4, 6 → 2 composites (Note: 4 = 2×2, 6 = 2×3)\n- **1** is **neither prime nor composite**\n\nSo we have:\n- Primes: 2, 3, 5 → probability of prime on one die = 3/6 = 1/2\n- Composites: 4, 6 → probability of composite = 2/6 = 1/3\n- Neither (1): 1/6 — but we are not allowing this in our desired outcome!\n\nThe question asks for **three dice show prime numbers** and **the rest (three) show composite numbers**. That means **no die can show 1** — that would violate the condition.\n\nSo we are restricted to outcomes where **each die is either prime or composite**, and **exactly three of each**.\n\nSo we must compute:\n\n- Number of ways to choose which 3 of the 6 dice show primes: $\\binom{6}{3}$\n- For each of those 3 dice: probability of prime = 3/6 = 1/2\n- For each of the other 3 dice: probability of composite = 2/6 = 1/3\n\nThus, the probability is:\n\n$$\n\\binom{6}{3} \\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^3 \\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)^3\n$$\n\nCompute:\n\n- $\\binom{6}{3} = 20$\n- $\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^3 = \\frac{1}{8}$\n- $\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)^3 = \\frac{1}{27}$\n\nMultiply:\n\n$$\n20 \\cdot \\frac{1}{8} \\cdot \\frac{1}{27} = \\frac{20}{216", "finish_reason": "length", "served_model": "qwen3-next-80b", "prompt_tokens": 198, "completion_tokens": 512, "total_tokens": 710, "reasoning_tokens": null, "headers": {"vsr_selected_model": "sclv/qwen3-next-80b", "vsr_response_path": "upstream"}, "extracted": "E", "correct": false}
