{"arm": "pinned:sclv/gemma-4", "requested_model": "sclv/gemma-4", "question_id": "8058", "dataset": "MMLU-Pro", "category": "math", "fold": "calibration", "started_at": 1787606244.4872582, "latency_ms": 3444.9067499954253, "http_status": 200, "attempts": 1, "error": null, "text": "To find the determinant of the matrix $A = \\begin{pmatrix} 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 7 & 8 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 5 & 4 \\end{pmatrix}$, we can use the expansion by minors along the first row.\n\nThe formula for the determinant of a $3 \\times 3$ matrix is:\n$\\det(A) = a(ei - fh) - b(di - fg) + c(dh - eg)$\n\nFor this matrix:\n$a = 0, b = 1, c = 2$\n$d = 7, e = 8, f = 3$\n$g = 6, h = 5, i = 4$\n\nSubstitute the values into the formula:\n$\\det(A) = 0(8 \\cdot 4 - 3 \\cdot 5) - 1(7 \\cdot 4 - 3 \\cdot 6) + 2(7 \\cdot 5 - 8 \\cdot 6)$\n\nCalculate each term:\n1. The first term is $0$.\n2. The second term: $-1(28 - 18) = -1(10) = -10$.\n3. The third term: $2(35 - 48) = 2(-13) = -26$.\n\nSum the results:\n$\\det(A) = 0 - 10 - 26 = -36$.\n\nComparing this result to the options:\nA) 0\nB) 24\nC) -12\nD) 36\nE) -48\nF) 72\nG) -60\nH) -24\nI) -36\nJ) 60\n\nThe result is -36, which corresponds to option I.\n\nAnswer: I", "finish_reason": "stop", "served_model": "gemma-4", "prompt_tokens": 181, "completion_tokens": 410, "total_tokens": 591, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "headers": {"vsr_selected_model": "sclv/gemma-4", "vsr_response_path": "upstream"}, "extracted": "I", "correct": true}
